{{!-- /the-faith-received/compare/ — the comparison desk.

     ROUTING. routes.yaml must map this template at
     /the-faith-received/compare/. The deploy Action does NOT ship
     routes.yaml (FRONTEND §6.12); it is uploaded by hand in Ghost
     Admin > Settings > Labs > Routes, and until it is, this URL 404s
     however healthy the template is.

     PORTED from the corpus owner's /compare. His interaction model is
     kept whole — authors as columns, the topic as the row, statements
     grouped by the work they came from, and the address as the view.
     His chrome is not: no second masthead, no bridge bar, no Google
     fonts, no inline :root palette. This page is .faith-received under
     the site's own header like every other Faith Received route.

     THE ADDRESS IS THE VIEW. #a=<slugs>&sel=<topic>&g=&s=&q= holds
     everything, so a comparison is linkable and a saved view is only a
     name and a hash. assets/js/page/faith-compare.js reads and writes
     it with replaceState.

     DOM contract for faith-compare.js. Every selector in that file:
       - [data-cmp-root] wrapping everything
       - [data-cmp-authors] — the chips
       - [data-cmp-add-form] > [data-cmp-add] + [data-cmp-add-list]
         (a datalist), and [data-cmp-add-note] for the four-author cap
       - [data-cmp-tools] holding [data-cmp-group], [data-cmp-stance],
         [data-cmp-phrase], [data-cmp-save], [data-cmp-export]
       - [data-cmp-topics-wrap] > [data-cmp-topics]
       - [data-cmp-topic-head], [data-cmp-columns]
       - [data-cmp-status] — the one status line
       - [data-cmp-empty] — shown only with no authors chosen
       - [data-cmp-saved] > [data-cmp-saved-count] + [data-cmp-saved-list]

     THE BACKEND. mo-tfr-library only, read from the tfr-library-base
     meta tag at the foot of this file. The owner's build called
     mo-tfr-ask-dev for its deep paging; that host appears nowhere here.
     The rooms, the full topic files and the topic export are all live
     on our worker today. GET /v1/evidence — the paging contract that
     reaches past the full file — is being built in a parallel session
     and 404s as of 2026-09-10, so the script probes it once and, when
     it is missing, says the rest of the index is not open yet and shows
     what it has. Nothing on this page waits on it. --}}

<main class="faith-received faith-feature">

  <section class="bhero bhero--tool">
    <div class="bhero-inner container">
      <p class="bhero-kicker"><a href="/the-faith-received/">The Faith Received</a> <span aria-hidden="true">&middot;</span> <a href="/the-faith-received/compare/">Compare</a></p>
      <h1>Compare</h1>
      <p class="bhero-sub">Set two to four authors beside each other on one topic and read what each of them actually says, grouped by the work it comes from.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="bband faith-feature-body faith-compare-band">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="research-workspace">
        <div class="research-workspace-inner" data-cmp-root>

          {{!-- The authors. Chips first, then the one control that adds
                another, because the set being compared is the thing the
                whole screen is about. --}}
          <div class="cmp-authorbar">
            <div class="cmp-authors" data-cmp-authors role="group" aria-label="Authors being compared"></div>

            <form class="cmp-add-form" data-cmp-add-form>
              <label class="cmp-add-label" for="cmp-add">Add an author</label>
              <input
                id="cmp-add"
                class="cmp-add"
                type="search"
                list="cmp-add-list"
                data-cmp-add
                maxlength="120"
                autocomplete="off"
                placeholder="An author&rsquo;s name&hellip;"
              />
              <datalist id="cmp-add-list" data-cmp-add-list></datalist>
              <button type="submit" class="cmp-add-submit">Add</button>
            </form>
            <p class="cmp-note" data-cmp-add-note hidden></p>
          </div>

          <p class="cmp-status" data-cmp-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>

          {{!-- The empty state. Named authors rather than a bare
                instruction: the hardest part of a comparison tool is
                the first move, and three real pairings that the library
                can actually answer are worth more than a sentence
                telling someone to start typing. These are links, so
                they cost nothing until pressed. --}}
          <div class="cmp-empty" data-cmp-empty>
            <p class="cmp-empty-lede">Nobody is being compared yet.</p>
            <p class="cmp-empty-note">Add an author above, then add a second. Two to four sit side by side, oldest first, so a topic reads as a reception history. Or begin with one of these:</p>
            <ul class="cmp-examples">
              <li><a href="/the-faith-received/compare/#a=augustine-of-hippo,jerome">Augustine and Jerome</a></li>
              <li><a href="/the-faith-received/compare/#a=ambrose-of-milan,augustine-of-hippo">Ambrose and Augustine</a></li>
              <li><a href="/the-faith-received/compare/#a=augustine-of-hippo,bede-the-venerable">Augustine and Bede</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          {{!-- The tools. Hidden until there is something to filter, so
                an empty screen is not fronted by five dead controls. --}}
          <div class="cmp-tools" data-cmp-tools hidden>
            <label class="cmp-field">
              <span class="cmp-field-label">Order works</span>
              <select class="cmp-select" data-cmp-group>
                <option value="work">Most statements first</option>
                <option value="canon">By title</option>
              </select>
            </label>
            <label class="cmp-field">
              <span class="cmp-field-label">Stance</span>
              <select class="cmp-select" data-cmp-stance>
                <option value="">Every stance</option>
                <option value="asserts">Asserts</option>
                <option value="denies">Denies</option>
                <option value="reports">Reports another view</option>
                <option value="qualifies">Qualifies or other</option>
              </select>
            </label>
            <label class="cmp-field cmp-field-wide">
              <span class="cmp-field-label">Phrase</span>
              <input class="cmp-input" type="search" data-cmp-phrase maxlength="120" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Find a phrase in every column&hellip;" />
            </label>
            <div class="cmp-tool-acts">
              <button type="button" class="cmp-act" data-cmp-save>Save this view</button>
              <button type="button" class="cmp-act cmp-act-primary" data-cmp-export>Send to the Desk</button>
            </div>
          </div>

          {{!-- The topics: the union of the chosen authors' own topics,
                each with every author's count beside it, so a topic only
                one of them treats is visible as exactly that rather
                than quietly absent. --}}
          <div class="cmp-topics-wrap" data-cmp-topics-wrap hidden>
            <details class="cmp-topics-fold" open>
              <summary class="cmp-topics-summary">
                <span class="cmp-topics-title">Choose a topic</span>
              </summary>
              <div class="cmp-topics" data-cmp-topics role="tablist" aria-label="Topics"></div>
            </details>
          </div>

          <div class="cmp-topic-head" data-cmp-topic-head></div>

          {{!-- One column per author. The grid is set from JS via
                --cmp-cols, since the count is 1 to 4 and only the script
                knows it. --}}
          <div class="cmp-columns" data-cmp-columns></div>

          {{!-- Saved views. An address and a name, kept in this browser,
                and the copy says so rather than implying an account. --}}
          <details class="cmp-saved" data-cmp-saved hidden>
            <summary class="cmp-saved-summary">
              <span class="cmp-saved-title">Saved comparisons</span>
              <span class="cmp-saved-count" data-cmp-saved-count></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="cmp-saved-body">
              <div data-cmp-saved-list></div>
              <p class="cmp-note">Saved comparisons are kept in this browser. They store the address of the view, not the passages, so re-opening one shows what the library holds today.</p>
            </div>
          </details>

          {{!-- Said once, at the foot, where it belongs: the whole
                screen is built on extracted statements and a reader who
                quotes one without opening the source can misattribute a
                view its author was arguing against. --}}
          <p class="cmp-caveat">These are extracted statements, sometimes summarised or translated, and not always direct quotations. A statement can report another speaker or a view its author rejects. Read the passage in its source before attributing it.</p>

        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
{{> "membership-cta"}}

<meta name="tfr-library-base" content="https://mo-tfr-library.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev" />
{{!-- The Desk's store first: Send to the Desk writes a draft through
     window.MOFaithDesk before redirecting, so it has to exist by the
